Dear National Archives of Singapore,

I run Lesser Known Singapore (https://pikaia.github.io and
https://www.youtube.com/@LesserKnownSingapore), a small non-commercial
blog covering overlooked history and lesser-known facts about
Singapore. I'd like to request permission to reproduce one photograph
from your online collection for an upcoming post about the history of
wild tigers in Singapore.

- "This tiger was shot by Tan Ah Mui (Chan Ah Mui) in the jungle at
  the 10th milestone off West Coast Road in the district of Pasir
  Panjang" =E2=80=94 Photo Accession No. 23192, Media/Image No.
  19980005489-0057, Tan Tuan Khoon Collection, covering date
  12 August 1928.

https://www.nas.gov.sg/archivesonline/photographs/record-details/2261b262-1=
162-11e3-83d5-0050568939ad

Intended use: an illustration in the post, which mentions this 1928
hunt (a relative of my wife's was, by family account, part of the
hunting party). Full credit would be given exactly as you advise, with
a link back to the record.

The record notes "use and reproduction only with permission." Could
you let me know the permissions, any rights-owner clearance I would
need to seek (the Tan Tuan Khoon Collection), the required credit
line, and any applicable fee for this non-commercial use? Happy to
provide any more detail on the post.

Thank you for your time.

Best regards,
Chris Lee
chriskslee@gmail.com
https://pikaia.github.io
https://www.youtube.com/@LesserKnownSingapore

